# Backend rules — expenses-tracking-backend

## Environment & package management
- **Node.js**: Use version `24.16.0` (see `.nvmrc`).
- **Always** use `pnpm` — never npm or yarn.

## NestJS structure
- One **feature module** per domain under `src/<feature>/` with `*.module.ts`, `*.service.ts`, and DTOs/inputs in `dto/`.
- GraphQL features use `*.resolver.ts` and object types in `models/`; REST features use `*.controller.ts`.
- Register new modules in `AppModule` imports.
- File names: **kebab-case** (`gql-auth.guard.ts`, `create-template.input.ts`).
- Class names: **PascalCase** (`TemplatesService`, `CreateTemplateInput`).

## Database (Prisma)
- All database access goes through an injectable **`PrismaService`** — never `new PrismaClient()` in controllers or services.
- After schema changes: `pnpm prisma migrate dev` then `pnpm prisma generate`.
- `User.id` must stay aligned with Supabase Auth UID (`sub`).

## Authentication
- **REST**: `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` and `@CurrentUser()`.
- **GraphQL**: `@UseGuards(GqlAuthGuard)` and `@CurrentUserGql()`; `GraphQLModule` must pass `context: ({ req }) => ({ req })`.
- JWT is issued by Supabase on the frontend; backend verifies via **`SUPABASE_URL` JWKS (ES256)** or legacy **`SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET` (HS256)**.
- Do not implement custom login endpoints — auth is delegated to Supabase.

## DTOs & validation
- Use request DTOs with `class-validator` decorators when adding validated REST endpoints.
- GraphQL uses `@InputType()` / `@ObjectType()` classes; avoid returning raw Prisma entities with sensitive fields.

## Configuration
- Read env vars via **`ConfigService`** (`@nestjs/config`), not `process.env` in services.
- Document new variables in `.env.example`.

## AI / DeepSeek integration
- Never trust the LLM to compute or return sums, totals, or amounts. Parse/merge raw input deterministically in code (see `src/ai/expense-file.parser.ts`), ask the LLM only for categorization/narrative text (`itemIds`, `savingsMessage`), then reconcile amounts back from the canonical parsed data (`src/ai/expense-analysis.reconciler.ts`).
- Format money via `src/ai/expense-amount.formatter.ts`, not ad-hoc `toLocaleString` calls, so PL/EN formatting stays consistent.

## Code style
- **Prettier**: single quotes, trailing commas.
- **Comments**: English for code; Polish is acceptable for user-facing API messages matching the product.
- **Tests**: unit tests co-located as `*.spec.ts`; E2E in `test/*.e2e-spec.ts`.

## Testing
- Run `pnpm run test` before finishing backend changes.
- Mock `PrismaService` and JWT guards in unit tests; use Supertest for E2E.

## Documentation
- Update `docs/architecture.md` or `docs/database.md` when adding modules or schema changes.
- See `AGENTS.md` for commands and project overview.
